# PASS1 annotations, keyed by object or storage address (development file).
# [names]     $addr NAME group MEANING      variables (storage address)
# [fns]       $addr NAME PARAM MEANING      DEF FN (body address)
# [routines]  $addr TITLE                   comment on a routine's first line
# [lines]     $addr COMMENT                 comment on the line starting at addr
[names]
$8F96 T    token   CURRENT TOKEN OR CHARACTER OF THE SOURCE LINE
$8FA4 NT   token   NEXT BYTE OF THE SOURCE LINE (ONE BYTE LOOKAHEAD); -1 AT END OF PROGRAM
$8FAA IB   token   BYTE JUST READ FROM THE SOURCE FILE
$8FC9 PL   token   LOW BYTE OF THE NEXT LINE LINK (A ZERO LINK ENDS THE PROGRAM)
$8F73 PB   token   BYTE WAITING TO BE COPIED INTO THE LISTING BUFFER
$8FBF BP   token   NEXT FREE BYTE IN THE LISTING BUFFER
$8F90 BS   token   START OF THE LISTING BUFFER ($0280)
$8FB2 BF   token   END OF THE LISTING BUFFER; A LINE THAT REACHES IT IS TOO LONG
$8FB6 LN   token   CURRENT SOURCE LINE NUMBER
$9009 DC   token   1 AFTER AN UNCONDITIONAL TRANSFER: FURTHER STATEMENTS ON THE LINE ARE NOT REACHED
$8FE2 TH   token   1 FOR THE STATEMENT RIGHT AFTER THEN (NO RESUME/DEBUG CALL)
$8FF7 DS   token   DECLARATION STATE: 2 BEFORE ANY STATEMENT, 1 AFTER COMMON, 0 AFTER A STATEMENT
$8FCF ID   token   2 WHILE NAMES ARE BEING DECLARED INTEGER (ALSO AFTER INTEGER *), ELSE 0
$900B SB   token   SAVED ID DURING AN INTEGER DECLARATION LIST
$8FBD FM   token   WHICH FILE DOS IS SET UP FOR: 1 SOURCE (READ), 2 OBJECT (WRITE), 3 LINE NUMBER FILE
$8F71 FW   token   1 TO WRITE TO THE LINE NUMBER FILE EVEN AFTER A FATAL ERROR
$94BD W$   token   WORK STRING: KEYWORD BEING MATCHED, DIGITS OF A NUMBER, NAME OF AN ERROR
$8FDA TK   stmt    TOKEN NUMBER OF THE STATEMENT (TOKEN-128), THEN THE CALL TABLE INDEX IT SELECTS
$8FE4 IL   stmt    1 IF THE FOR LOOP VARIABLE IS AN INTEGER
$8F92 SV   stmt    SAVED SYMBOL (FOR LOOP VARIABLE), OR THE NUMBER OF LINES IN AN ON LIST
$8FF1 ND   stmt    NUMBER OF DIMENSIONS IN A DIM OR DECLARATION
$8FD1 BB   stmt    START OF THE TEXT OF A STRING LITERAL OR DATA ITEM IN THE LISTING BUFFER
$8F9C XT   stmt    TOKEN OR CHARACTER EXPECTED NEXT (SYNTAX CHECK)
$8F9E FH   stmt    INSIDE DEF FN: NAME HASH OF THE PARAMETER, ELSE 0
$8FA8 PM   stmt    INSIDE DEF FN: THE PARAMETER'S SYMBOL
$8FFD PA   stmt    ADDRESS TO PATCH WITH THE CURRENT CODE ADDRESS
$8FB0 HA   symbol  NAME HASH (99*FIRST CHARACTER+SECOND), OR LINE NUMBER-32767
$8FC7 K    symbol  TYPE CODE (-3 REAL, -2 STRING, -1 INTEGER, +22 FOR AN ARRAY), OR AN OPERATION NUMBER
$8F79 V    symbol  VALUE PASSED TO AND FROM THE STACK AND SYMBOL ROUTINES (USUALLY A SYMBOL)
$8FA6 NF   symbol  NEXT FREE WORD IN THE SYMBOL TABLE {SY}()
$8FD8 SL   symbol  SIZE OF THE SYMBOL TABLE (5350 WORDS)
$8FD3 N    symbol  NUMERIC VALUE OF A LINE NUMBER, DIMENSION OR CONSTANT
$9003 NG   symbol  1 IF THE LAST SCAN FOUND NO NAME OR NO NUMBER
$8FCD Q    symbol  SCRATCH: A SYMBOL OR SIZE BEING WORKED ON
$8FC5 M    symbol  SCRATCH
$8FE0 I    symbol  LOOP INDEX
$8FED J    symbol  INNER LOOP INDEX; 1 IF AN ARRAY WAS DIMENSIONED BEFORE
$8F98 TP   parse   OPERATOR ON TOP OF THE PARSE STACK
$8F9A SP   parse   NEXT FREE PLACE FOR AN OPERATOR ON THE PARSE STACK (GROWS UP)
$8FCB VP   parse   NEXT FREE PLACE FOR AN OPERAND ON THE PARSE STACK (GROWS DOWN)
$8FA2 SZ   parse   SIZE OF THE PARSE STACK (100)
$8FEF EE   parse   1 WHEN THE EXPRESSION IS COMPLETE
$8FF9 BY   parse   1 IF THE OPERATOR BEING REDUCED TAKES TWO OPERANDS
$9005 ET   parse   TYPE OF THE EXPRESSION: 1 INTEGER, 2 STRING, 3 REAL
$8FAE TC   triple  NUMBER OF TRIPLES IN {TR}() PLUS ONE
$8FDE TL   triple  SIZE OF THE TRIPLE TABLE (100)
$8FFF TX   triple  TRIPLE BEING GENERATED
$9007 SX   triple  TRIPLE BEING EXAMINED WHEN DECIDING WHERE A RESULT GOES
$8FE6 OC   triple  OPERATION CODE OF THE TRIPLE
$9001 OV   triple  OPERATION CODE USED TO SELECT THE GENERATOR, OR A SUBSCRIPT COUNT
$8FF5 LX   triple  LEFT OPERAND OF THE TRIPLE
$8FFB RX   triple  RIGHT OPERAND OF THE TRIPLE
$8F8C OX   triple  OPERAND BEING LOADED OR APPLIED
$8F81 KD   triple  KIND OF THAT OPERAND (ITS {TR}(X,0) ENTRY)
$8F7D RO   triple  1 IF THE OPERANDS ARE USED AS REALS
$8F94 RR   triple  1 IF THE RESULT IS REAL
$8FDC FL   triple  1 IF THE FLAGS ALREADY REFLECT THE RESULT (IF NEEDS NO TEST)
$8F88 FS   triple  WHICH FLAG TEST IF NEEDS: 0 INTEGER (LDA $A0/ORA $A1), 1 REAL (LDA $9D)
$900D VK   triple  OPERATION NUMBER FOR A MEMORY OPERAND, OR THE OPERAND SAVED FOR LATER
$8FC3 XI   triple  CALL TABLE INDEX FOR THE OPERANDS IN THE OTHER ORDER (SWAPPED COMPARISON)
$8FF3 SG   triple  1 WHEN THE RESULT IS STORED THROUGH AN ARRAY ELEMENT ADDRESS
$8F77 TS   triple  1 WHEN THE EXPRESSION IS THE VALUE OF AN ASSIGNMENT
$8FA0 LK   triple  OPERATION OF THE LAST TRIPLE (TELLS THE STORE WHAT IS IN THE ACCUMULATOR)
$8FAC RS   triple  SYMBOL OF THE EXPRESSION'S RESULT
$8F7F SK   triple  SAVED OPERATION NUMBER
$8F8E SC   triple  SAVED OPERATION NUMBER
$8FB4 LV   emit    LAST VARIABLE STORED BY THE CODE (A LOAD RIGHT AFTER IT IS LEFT OUT)
$8F75 SA   emit    CODE ADDRESS OF THAT STORE
$8FBB CI   emit    INDEX OF THE ROUTINE IN THE CALL TABLE {CT}()
$8F8A EA   emit    ENTRY ADJUSTMENT: 0, OR -3 FOR THE OTHER TYPE'S ENTRY
$8FC1 WT   emit    TYPE THE CALL TABLE ENTRY IS FOR: 1 INTEGER, 3 REAL
$8F7B OB   emit    BYTE TO WRITE TO THE OBJECT FILE
$8F83 W    emit    WORD TO WRITE TO THE OBJECT FILE (A LINK OR ADDRESS)
$8FE8 HB   emit    HIGH BYTE OF THAT WORD
$900F OT   tables  OPERATOR TABLE: {OT}(I,0) TOKEN, {OT}(I,1) PRIORITY ON THE STACK, {OT}(I,2) PRIORITY ARRIVING
$9075 FA   tables  ARGUMENT DESCRIPTION OF A FUNCTION: {FA}(0) NUMBER, {FA}(1..3) TYPES, {FA}(4) ARGUMENT BEING READ
$907F ST   tables  PARSE STACK: OPERATORS FROM THE BOTTOM, OPERANDS FROM THE TOP
$9149 TR   tables  TRIPLE TABLE: {TR}(I,0) OPERATION OR OPERAND KIND, {TR}(I,1) LEFT, {TR}(I,2) RIGHT
$93AD CT   tables  CALL TABLE: ADDRESSES OF THE LIBRARY AND ROM ROUTINES, BY INDEX
[fns]
$42EC LT X  TRUE IF X IS A LETTER
$430B DG X  TRUE IF X IS A DIGIT
$432A OS X  TRUE IF X IS AN OPERATOR TOKEN (+ - * / ^ AND OR > = < NOT, OR A TWO-CHARACTER RELATION)
$436D OE X  TRUE IF X IS AN OPERATOR, A PARENTHESIS OR THE END OF THE LINE
$43AD NU X  TRUE IF X IS A NUMERIC FUNCTION TOKEN (SGN TO LEN, VAL, ASC)
$43F0 SF X  TRUE IF X IS A STRING FUNCTION TOKEN (STR$, CHR$, LEFT$, RIGHT$, MID$)
$4421 ES X  TRUE IF X ENDS A STATEMENT (COLON OR END OF LINE)
$4440 UB X  X STORED AS A WORD (X+32767)
$444A IV X  TRUE IF TRIPLE X GIVES AN INTEGER (INTEGER TEMPORARY, INTEGER VARIABLE OR RESULT)
$44BD LO X  TRUE IF OPERATION X TAKES ITS LEFT OPERAND FROM THE ACCUMULATOR
$44EE RT X  TRUE IF OPERATION X TAKES ITS RIGHT OPERAND FROM THE ACCUMULATOR
$4543 IA X  TRUE IF TRIPLE X IS IN THE ACCUMULATOR
[routines]
$4206 PASS 1 OF THE COMPILER: READS THE TOKENIZED SOURCE PROGRAM A BYTE AT A TIME, CHECKS ITS SYNTAX, BUILDS THE SYMBOL TABLE IN {SY}() AND WRITES THE OBJECT CODE. REFERENCES THAT ARE NOT YET KNOWN (LINES, VARIABLE ROUTINES) ARE WRITTEN AS BACKWARD CHAINS FOR PASS 2. SET UP THE BUFFERS AND TABLES
$4635 START: THE CODE BEGINS 20 BYTES INTO THE PROGRAM (AFTER THE CALL TO THE LIBRARY AND THE HEADER); READ THE FIRST LINE'S LINK AND NUMBER
$46B9 STATEMENT LOOP: START A NEW LINE
$46BC NEXT STATEMENT ON THE LINE
$47FB END: JMP TO THE LIBRARY'S END ROUTINE; WHAT FOLLOWS ON THE LINE IS NOT REACHED
$4801 FOR V=E1 TO E2 [STEP E3]: INITIAL VALUE (WITH THE LOOP VARIABLE'S ADDRESS), LIMIT, STEP; INTEGER LOOPS USE THE INTEGER ENTRIES
$489D NEXT [V[,V]...]: ONE CALL PER VARIABLE, EACH FOLLOWED BY THE VARIABLE'S ADDRESS (0 FOR A BARE NEXT)
$48CE DATA: JUMP OVER THE ITEMS, EACH STORED AS LENGTH AND TEXT, ENDED BY 255 AND A LINK TO THE NEXT DATA BLOCK
$499D INPUT ["PROMPT";] V[,V]...
$4A2A DIM: SET THE DIMENSIONS OF EACH ARRAY (CONSTANTS ONLY); NO CODE
$4A39 READ A DIMENSION LIST INTO THE SYMBOL'S ENTRY; AN ARRAY MAY BE DIMENSIONED ONLY ONCE AND BEFORE IT IS USED WITH A DIFFERENT NUMBER OF SUBSCRIPTS
$4B80 READ V[,V]...
$4BC4 PLOT X,Y / HLIN X1,X2 AT Y / VLIN Y1,Y2 AT X
$4BFC HPLOT [TO] X,Y [TO X,Y]...
$4C43 DRAW / XDRAW SHAPE [AT X,Y]
$4C7E ONERR GOTO LINE: CALL WITH THE HANDLER'S ADDRESS; WHAT FOLLOWS ON THE LINE IS NOT REACHED
$4C93 RESUME: A JUMP TO THE LIBRARY ONLY WITH THE RESUME/DEBUG OPTION, OTHERWISE IGNORED WITH A WARNING
$4CA4 LET (ALSO A STATEMENT THAT BEGINS WITH A NAME): COMPILE THE TARGET, THEN THE EXPRESSION OF ITS TYPE, THEN THE STORE
$4CCF IF ... THEN LINE / GOTO LINE: BEQ OVER A JMP TO THE LINE
$4CE4 GOTO LINE: JMP TO THE LINE (CHAINED UNTIL PASS 2 KNOWS ITS ADDRESS)
$4CF3 RUN: JMP $03F5 (THE & VECTOR, WHICH THE LIBRARY POINTS AT THE PROGRAM); RUN LINE: CLEAR, THEN GOTO
$4D1E IF EXPRESSION THEN ...: SET THE FLAGS FROM THE RESULT, THEN DECIDE THE FORM
$4DA2 GOSUB LINE: JSR TO THE LINE
$4DB1 IF ... THEN RETURN: BEQ OVER AN RTS
$4DC6 RETURN: RTS
$4DCF AFTER AN UNCONDITIONAL TRANSFER: THE REST OF THE LINE IS NOT REACHED
$4DD8 REM: REM! STARTS A COMPILER DIRECTIVE, ANY OTHER REMARK IS SKIPPED
$4E73 REM! CLEAR COMMON / REM! CLEAR CHAIN: A CALL TO THE LIBRARY; MUST END THE LINE
$4EE9 REM! USECOMMON / REM! DEFCOMMON LIST: ALLOCATE THE COMMON BLOCK AT THE PROGRAM START IN DECLARATION ORDER AND MOVE THE PROGRAM START UP
$5090 AFTER A NAME IN A DECLARATION LIST: A COMMA CONTINUES IT, THE END OF THE LINE ENDS IT
$50DE MATCH THE KEYWORD IN {W$} AGAINST THE SOURCE, LETTER BY LETTER (SPACES ALLOWED); A MISMATCH IGNORES THE REST OF THE REMARK
$5141 SKIP SPACES
$5156 STOP / NEW: CALL THE LIBRARY; WHAT FOLLOWS ON THE LINE IS NOT REACHED
$515C ON EXPRESSION GOTO / GOSUB LINE[,LINE]...: CALL WITH THE COUNT AND THE LINE ADDRESSES
$51CF WAIT ADDRESS,MASK[,MASK]
$520A DEF FN NAME(PARAMETER)=EXPRESSION: JUMP OVER THE BODY; THE BODY STORES THE ARGUMENT IN THE PARAMETER, COMPUTES THE EXPRESSION AND RETURNS
$52AD POKE ADDRESS,VALUE
$52C2 PRINT: EACH ITEM BY TYPE; ; NOTHING, , A TAB TO THE NEXT FIELD, TAB( AND SPC( CALLS; A CARRIAGE RETURN UNLESS THE STATEMENT ENDS WITH ; , TAB( OR SPC(
$5382 GET V
$53B1 EXPECT A COMMA, ELSE THE STATEMENT IS FINISHED
$53CB CALL / HIMEM: (ONE ARGUMENT, REAL ENTRY)
$53DD STATEMENTS WITH ONE ARGUMENT: VTAB HTAB COLOR= HCOLOR= SPEED= ROT= SCALE= IN# PR#
$53EF POP / CLEAR / STATEMENTS WITHOUT ARGUMENTS
$53F5 END OF THE STATEMENT: LIST THE LINE IF ASKED, CHECK FOR CONTROL-C, GO ON WITH THE NEXT STATEMENT OR LINE
$5476 END OF THE PROGRAM: PATCH THE REFERENCES STILL WAITING ON THE STACK, CLOSE THE FILES AND RUN PASS 2
$54D8 WARNING: LINE NUMBER N IGNORED (AN UNSUPPORTED KEYWORD, OR A STATEMENT AFTER AN UNCONDITIONAL TRANSFER); SKIP TO THE NEXT COLON OUTSIDE QUOTES
$5545 SKIP TO THE NEXT COLON OUTSIDE QUOTES OR THE END OF THE LINE
$5597 EXPECT = / ( / ) / , / THE CHARACTER IN {XT}; ELSE A SYNTAX ERROR
$55C6 FATAL ERRORS: NAME THE KIND IN {W$}
$56BE REPORT A FATAL ERROR, SHOW THE LINE WITH !ERR!, PAUSE IF ASKED; NO MORE CODE IS WRITTEN
$5807 CONVERT THE DIGITS IN {W$} TO A NUMBER (A BAD NUMBER SETS {NG})
$584F LIST THE LINE IN THE LISTING BUFFER
$5877 NEXT TOKEN: {T} = NEXT BYTE OF THE LINE, {NT} = THE ONE AFTER IT, COPYING EACH INTO THE LISTING BUFFER
$5885 START A LINE: READ ITS NUMBER, DEFINE ITS LINE SYMBOL AT THE CURRENT CODE ADDRESS, RECORD IT IN THE LINE NUMBER FILE
$59BA READ ONE BYTE OF THE SOURCE FILE INTO {IB}
$59FC LINE NUMBER REFERENCE: FIND OR ENTER THE LINE'S SYMBOL
$5AB1 SCAN A NUMBER INTO {W$}
$5AFD NAME WITH ITS TYPE AND SUBSCRIPTS: AN OPERAND
$5B15 NAME WITH ITS TYPE SUFFIX: {K} = -1 FOR %, -2 FOR $, ELSE -3
$5B68 SCAN A NAME: {HA} = 99*FIRST CHARACTER+SECOND; LATER LETTERS AND DIGITS ARE SKIPPED
$5BD5 ARRAY ELEMENT: SUBSCRIPTS AS EXPRESSIONS, CHECKED AGAINST THE ARRAY'S DIMENSIONS
$5D7C FUNCTION ARGUMENTS, AS DESCRIBED IN {FA}()
$5EF1 STRING LITERAL: JUMP OVER ITS LENGTH AND TEXT; THE CODE REFERS TO IT BY ADDRESS
$5FAE EXPRESSIONS: PARSE INTO TRIPLES, THEN GENERATE THE CODE ({ET} GIVES THE TYPE)
$5FE4 PARSER: BOTTOM UP WITH THE OPERATOR AND OPERAND STACK; OPERANDS AND REDUCED OPERATORS BECOME TRIPLES IN {TR}()
$6255 NUMERIC CONSTANT: AN INTEGER IF INTEGER CONSTANTS ARE ON AND THE VALUE IS A WHOLE NUMBER UP TO 32767, ELSE REAL, PACKED BY THE USR ROUTINE; ENTERED IN ITS CONSTANT CHAIN (VALUE OR EXPONENT MOD 32)
$63FB NUMERIC FUNCTION CALL (SGN TO LEN, VAL, ASC)
$64C2 FN NAME(ARGUMENT)
$6702 TWO-CHARACTER RELATIONS: >= OR => (235), <= OR =< (236), <> OR >< (237)
$67AB REDUCE WHILE THE OPERATOR ON THE STACK HAS A HIGHER PRIORITY THAN THE ONE ARRIVING ({OT}())
$6A1A PARSE STACK: PUSH AN OPERATOR, POP, PUSH AND POP AN OPERAND
$6AC8 STORE A TRIPLE IN {TR}()
$6B16 VARIABLE SYMBOL: FIND OR ENTER THE NAME IN CHAIN (HASH+TYPE) MOD 32, AT THE END OF THE CHAIN; INSIDE DEF FN THE PARAMETER'S NAME MEANS THE PARAMETER
$6C56 FN AND LINE SYMBOLS (CHAINS 1-4)
$6D06 ALLOCATE {M} WORDS OF THE SYMBOL TABLE
$6D4F EMIT A VARIABLE OR CONSTANT ROUTINE CALL: MARK THE OPERATION USED, WRITE THE OPERATION NUMBER AND LINK THE REFERENCE INTO THE SYMBOL'S CHAIN
$6DED EMIT AN OPCODE AND A CHAINED REFERENCE (LINE OR FN)
$6E08 EMIT A WORD
$6E3B EMIT A BYTE
$6E7A WRITE TO THE LINE NUMBER FILE / PATCH A WORD IN THE OBJECT FILE
$6F23 FILE HELPERS
$6F9E RESUME/DEBUG: A CALL TO THE LIBRARY'S DEBUG ROUTINE BEFORE THE STATEMENT, EXCEPT RIGHT AFTER THEN
$6FC8 EMIT A JSR TO CALL TABLE ENTRY {CI}; THE ENTRY 3 BYTES LOWER SERVES THE OTHER ARGUMENT TYPE
$7000 EMIT A JMP TO CALL TABLE ENTRY {CI}
$7021 TEMPORARIES: TAKE THE FIRST FREE ONE OF THE TYPE FROM ITS CHAIN (5 INTEGER, 6 STRING, 7 REAL, 8 ALL TYPES INSIDE DEF FN), ELSE MAKE A NEW ONE
$70B6 FREE A TEMPORARY
$70CF END OF DEF FN: THE FUNCTION'S TEMPORARIES ARE NOT USED AGAIN
$7135 GENERATE THE CODE OF AN ASSIGNMENT'S VALUE
$715A CODE GENERATOR: FOR EACH TRIPLE, DECIDE WHETHER ITS OPERANDS ARE INTEGER OR REAL, THEN GENERATE IT; A RESULT THAT IS NOT USED BY THE NEXT TRIPLE GOES TO A TEMPORARY
$7439 BY OPERATION
$74BA + * : APPLY THE OPERAND IN MEMORY TO THE ACCUMULATOR
$7555 AND / OR: TEST THE OPERAND IN MEMORY (LDA, AND ORA FOR AN INTEGER), THEN CALL
$75ED COMPARISONS: IF THE RIGHT OPERAND IS IN THE ACCUMULATOR, COMPARE WITH THE LEFT ONE AND USE THE OPPOSITE RELATION
$765F ARRAY ELEMENT: PUSH ALL SUBSCRIPTS BUT THE FIRST, LAST TO FIRST
$7726 STRING COMPARISONS, LIKEWISE
$7834 WHERE DOES THE RESULT GO: THE NEXT TRIPLE THAT USES IT, OR A TEMPORARY
$7972 A STRING RESULT IS KEPT IF THE NEXT STRING OPERATION USES IT, ELSE SAVED IN A STRING TEMPORARY
$7B9F STORE THE RESULT OF AN EXPRESSION IN THE TARGET
$7C5A LOAD OR APPLY AN OPERAND
$7DF9 SET THE FLAGS FOR IF
$7E1C COMPILATION TERMINATED: DELETE THE OBJECT FILE AND RESTORE DOS
[lines]
$422C THE LISTING BUFFER IS THE INPUT BUFFER $0280-$036F
$4277 COPY THE CALL TABLE OUT OF THE COMMON SYMBOL TABLE AREA WHERE PASS 0 LEFT IT
$429F COPY THE OPERATOR TABLE LIKEWISE
$46C2 COLON OR END OF LINE: AN EMPTY STATEMENT
$46CF ANY STATEMENT BUT REM ENDS THE DECLARATIONS
$46E3 NOT A KEYWORD: AN ASSIGNMENT
$4703 NOT REACHED: SKIP IT WITH A WARNING (DATA AND REM ARE STILL COMPILED)
$4744 DISPATCH ON THE KEYWORD
$4D78 IF ... THEN STATEMENTS: BNE OVER A JMP TO THE NEXT LINE
$4D99 THE STATEMENT AFTER THEN GETS NO RESUME/DEBUG CALL
$4EA3 CLEAR COMMON OR CLEAR CHAIN
$5421 CONTROL-C TERMINATES THE COMPILATION
$54B4 RUN PASS 2
$6D3A SYMBOL TABLE FULL?
$6F3F KEEP THE DRIVE RUNNING IF ALL FILES ARE ON THE BOOT DRIVE
$7D69 A LOAD (OR AND/OR TEST) OF THE VARIABLE JUST STORED IS LEFT OUT WHEN THE STORE WAS THE LAST CODE WRITTEN
